/* Wang, Fu, Goharshady, Chatterjee, Qin and Shi, "Cost Analysis of Nondeterministic Probabilistic
   Programs", PLDI 2019, Fig. 3 (Bitcoin mining), negative (reward) part of the cost from x = 100:
   each round, with probability p = 0.0005 the puzzle is solved; then with probability p' = 0.99 the
   reward 5000 is paid, and otherwise a nondeterministic choice decides between the reward and
   nothing.  This file asks an upper bound over all schedulers, so the scheduler grants the
   reward (max); exact value 250 = 2.5 per round.
   The files wang19_fig3_neg_{lb,ub}.qhes pay the reward on both arms of that choice (the
   reward-granting scheduler); this one keeps the choice as in the paper. */
X 100.0 <= 250.0
s.t.
X (x : real) : real =mu
  if x >= 1.0 then
    0.0005 * (0.99 * (X (x - 1.0) + 5000.0) + 0.01 * max (X (x - 1.0) + 5000.0) (X (x - 1.0))) +
    0.9995 * X (x - 1.0)
  else 0.0;
